  <data name="MainPage.NavigationBar.Title.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>MailFathom</value>
    <comment>The product name. It is the same in every language: a name is not translated.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SettingsPage.TextBlock.Deployment.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Połączono z</value>
    <comment>Labels the address of the MailFathom deployment this client reaches. Phrased as the relationship rather than as "Deployment address", which names a setting instead of saying where you are.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SettingsPage.Button.ChangeDeployment.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Użyj innego MailFathom</value>
    <comment>Opens the screen that asks for a deployment address. Named for what a person wants rather than for the setting it changes.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectPage.NavigationBar.Title.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Twój MailFathom</value>
    <comment>Titles the screen that asks which deployment this client reaches. Possessive, because a deployment is somebody's own server rather than a service they sign up to.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectPage.TextBlock.Lead.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>MailFathom działa na serwerze, który należy do Ciebie. Podaj tej aplikacji adres swojego, a od teraz będzie się od niego zaczynać.</value>
    <comment>Says why the screen is asking, for somebody who has just installed the client and may not know that no address is assumed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectPage.TextBlock.Address.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Adres</value>
    <comment>Labels the box the deployment address is written in, for a reader and for a screen reader.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectPage.TextBox.Address.PlaceholderText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>mail.example.com</value>
    <comment>An example of the shape rather than a suggestion: it is a reserved example domain, so nobody reaches anything by leaving it as it is.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectPage.TextBlock.AddressHint.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Sam adres, bez niczego po nim. Zapisany bez https:// jest odczytywany jako https://.</value>
    <comment>States the two things about the shape somebody could otherwise only learn from a refusal: no path, and what an omitted scheme means.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectPage.Button.Connect.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Połącz</value>
    <comment>Takes the address written above and checks that a MailFathom answers there. Phrased as the act, and nothing is kept unless it succeeds.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectPage.InfoBar.Refusal.Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Brak połączenia</value>
    <comment>Heads the sentence explaining why an address was not taken. States the outcome; the message beside it states the cause.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectPage.Refusal.NotAnAddress" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>To nie jest adres. Wpisz nazwę serwera, na przykład mail.example.com.</value>
    <comment>Shown when the text cannot be read as an address at all. Repeats the shape rather than the text, which the person can still see.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectPage.Refusal.ClearTextOffThisMachine" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ten adres nie jest zabezpieczony. Wszystko, co ta aplikacja wysyła, niesie Twoje logowanie, więc wpisz adres https://.</value>
    <comment>Shown for clear text to anything but this machine. Says why rather than only that it is refused, because the person chose http:// deliberately.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectPage.Refusal.MoreThanAnOrigin" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Wpisz sam adres, bez niczego po nim — bez ścieżki i bez wpisanego w niego logowania.</value>
    <comment>Shown when the address carries a path, a query, a fragment, or embedded credentials.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectPage.Refusal.Unreachable" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Pod tym adresem nic nie odpowiedziało. Sprawdź, czy jest poprawny i czy to urządzenie ma połączenie.</value>
    <comment>Shown when the connection failed outright. Names both causes, because from here they are indistinguishable.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectPage.Refusal.TimedOut" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ten adres nie odpowiedział na czas. Spróbuj ponownie za chwilę.</value>
    <comment>Shown when something is there and was too slow. Worth retrying unchanged, which is what separates it from the message above.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectPage.Refusal.NotADeployment" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Coś tam odpowiedziało, ale to nie jest MailFathom. Sprawdź adres.</value>
    <comment>Shown when the answer was not MailFathom's own — a captive portal, a proxy, or another service on the port.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignInPage.NavigationBar.Title.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Logowanie</value>
    <comment>Titles the screen that asks who somebody is on the deployment this client reaches.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignInPage.TextBlock.Lead.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Użyj nazwy użytkownika i hasła, które otrzymałeś od osoby prowadzącej Twój MailFathom. To nie jest hasło do żadnej skrzynki pocztowej, którą ten serwer czyta.</value>
    <comment>Says which credential is being asked for, because a mail application asking for a password is otherwise read as asking for the mail account's own.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignInPage.TextBlock.Username.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Nazwa użytkownika</value>
    <comment>Labels the box the username is written in, for a reader and for a screen reader.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignInPage.TextBox.Username.PlaceholderText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>twoja nazwa użytkownika</value>
    <comment>An example of the shape rather than a suggestion, since a username is whatever an administrator issued.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignInPage.TextBlock.Password.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Hasło</value>
    <comment>Labels the box the password is written in, for a reader and for a screen reader.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignInPage.Button.SignIn.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Zaloguj się</value>
    <comment>Offers what has been typed to the deployment. Phrased as the act, and nothing is kept unless it is accepted.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignInPage.InfoBar.Keeping.Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Następnym razem</value>
    <comment>Heads the sentence saying what this device does with the sign-in once it is accepted. States the subject; the message beside it states what happens.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignInPage.Keeping.NotOfferedOnThisHead" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>W przeglądarce zalogujesz się ponownie przy każdej wizycie. Cokolwiek działa na tej stronie mogłoby odczytać zapisane hasło, więc nic nie jest zapisywane.</value>
    <comment>Shown on the browser head, where every store is scoped to the page's origin rather than to a person. Says why rather than only that, because it is a property of browsers rather than of this application.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignInPage.Keeping.StoreUnavailable" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>To urządzenie nie ma pęku kluczy, do którego aplikacja mogłaby sięgnąć, więc przy następnym uruchomieniu zalogujesz się ponownie.</value>
    <comment>Shown where the operating system's own secret store is absent, locked, or refusing — a Linux session with no keyring is the ordinary case. Nothing weaker is written instead.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignInPage.InfoBar.Refusal.Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Nie zalogowano</value>
    <comment>Heads the sentence explaining why a sign-in was not accepted. States the outcome; the message beside it states the cause.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignInPage.Refusal.NotACredential" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Wpisz nazwę użytkownika i hasło. Nazwa użytkownika nie może zawierać dwukropka.</value>
    <comment>Shown when what was typed could not be presented at all — one half blank, or a colon in the username, which HTTP Basic would read as the start of the password.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignInPage.Refusal.CredentialRefused" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ta nazwa użytkownika i hasło nie zostały przyjęte. Sprawdź obie wartości i spróbuj ponownie.</value>
    <comment>Shown when the deployment refused the credential. Names the pair rather than one half, because the deployment deliberately does not say which was wrong.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignInPage.Refusal.PasswordSignInNotOffered" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ten MailFathom nie przyjmuje nazwy użytkownika i hasła. Poproś osobę, która go prowadzi, o włączenie logowania hasłem.</value>
    <comment>Shown when the deployment's refusal invited no password at all. Sends the person to their operator rather than to their own password, which was never the problem.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignInPage.Refusal.Unreachable" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Nic nie odpowiedziało pod tym adresem. Sprawdź, czy to urządzenie ma połączenie z siecią.</value>
    <comment>Shown when the connection failed outright. The address itself was already proved reachable when it was chosen, so this is about now.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignInPage.Refusal.TimedOut" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Twój MailFathom nie odpowiedział na czas. Spróbuj ponownie za chwilę.</value>
    <comment>Shown when something is there and was too slow. Worth retrying unchanged, which is what separates it from the message above.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignInPage.Refusal.NotADeployment" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Coś odpowiedziało, ale nie tak jak MailFathom. Sprawdź adres na poprzednim ekranie.</value>
    <comment>Shown when the answer was not MailFathom's own — a captive portal, a proxy, or another service that has taken the port since the address was chosen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SettingsPage.TextBlock.SignedInAs.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Zalogowano jako</value>
    <comment>Labels the username this client is signed in under. Phrased as the relationship rather than as "Username", which names a field instead of saying who you are.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SettingsPage.TextBlock.SignOutIsLocal.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Wylogowanie usuwa dane logowania z tego urządzenia. Twoje hasło pozostaje ważne, dopóki nie zmieni go osoba prowadząca Twój MailFathom.</value>
    <comment>Says what signing out does and does not do, because a sign-out control is otherwise read as revoking the credential.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SettingsPage.Button.SignOut.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Wyloguj się</value>
    <comment>Ends the session on this device and clears whatever it kept of it. Named for the act rather than for the storage it empties.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SettingsPage.TextBlock.Language.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Język</value>
    <comment>Labels the control that chooses which language the application is read in, for a reader and for a screen reader.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SettingsPage.Button.ApplyLanguage.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Użyj tego języka</value>
    <comment>Takes the language selected beside it. Phrased as the act rather than as "OK", because nothing is undone by leaving the screen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SettingsPage.InfoBar.LanguageRestart.Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Język zapisany</value>
    <comment>Shown once a language has been taken. Saved rather than changed, because the words on screen have not changed yet.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SettingsPage.InfoBar.LanguageRestart.Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>MailFathom będzie w wybranym języku przy następnym uruchomieniu.</value>
    <comment>Says plainly that the choice takes effect on the next launch, which is when Uno applies a culture.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SettingsPage.TextBlock.Theme.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Motyw</value>
    <comment>Labels the control that chooses whether the application is shown light, dark, or the way the system is set.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="AppTheme.System" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Zgodnie z systemem</value>
    <comment>One of the three theme offers. Phrased as what it does rather than as "System", which reads as a place.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="AppTheme.Light" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Jasny</value>
    <comment>One of the three theme offers.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="AppTheme.Dark" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ciemny</value>
    <comment>One of the three theme offers.</comment>
  </data>
